From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:06:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc TIPS screen from the original Game.exe
 (TipsSystemType / TipsMenuType SGHD)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The STEINS;GATE (Steam) TIPS data and screen as the original reads, draws and handles them, instead of no TIPS at
all (TipsSystemType.None: tips were never unlocked and the screen showed nothing until Back). Data format, sorting,
layout and behaviour come from the original Game.exe: TipsDataInit 0x43e100 (with the sort key 0x43e060), TipsInit
0x43f050, the draw routine 0x43e440 and the main routine 0x43f720.

- New TipsSystemType.SGHD (SGHD::TipsSystem): records from the first data label of _TIPS (content count, base
  string; strings base + 0..3 are label, name, second line, reading, base + 4 + i the content), letter and category
  tables from the second label (letters string, sort string, sort character -> letter, letter -> category). Tips are
  numbered in reading order (sort string order, shorter first); every category lists its tips with a letter header
  before the first tip of each letter. Lock / unread / new states use the save system's tip status bits.
- TipsDataInit keeps the second data label (TipsSystem::AuxDataAdr) instead of discarding it.
- New TipsMenuType.SGHD (UI::SGHD::TipsMenu), all positions, sizes, colours and string numbers in the profile:
  categories (empty ones blue) plus NEW (the tips found last first) and UNREAD lists, NEW marks; the tips of a
  category with 【letter】 headers over the header bar, number, separator and name (green while unread, "???" in grey
  while locked); the chosen tip on the right (number, name and second line right aligned, label, content in the TIPS
  text mode, clipped, L1 / R1 by pages, wheel); scrollbar knobs; the button guide. Shown while the script's submenu
  is TIPS (opacity SW_SYSSUBMENUCT * SW_SYSSUBMENUALPHA / 16), opens on the last shown tip (script variable 2316),
  Back in the tips list returns to the categories, in the categories it is left to the script.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15, original English data): TIPS from the title EXTRA list and from the in-game system menu;
category list matches screenshots of the original; after playing on, unlocked tips appear with NEW marks, the NEW list
opens with its 【New】 header, a tip shows its number, name, second line, label and content, R1 scrolls the content,
Back returns to the categories and closes the screen.

